1
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:31,040
It's coming from the courtyard.

2
00:03:37,470 --> 00:03:39,030
It's the Lord Commander!

3
00:03:52,290 --> 00:03:53,520
Help me get him inside.

4
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:50,940
Thorne did this.

5
00:04:55,950 --> 00:04:58,270
How many of your brothers do you think you can trust?

6
00:04:59,270 --> 00:05:00,150
Trust?

7
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,960
The men in this room.

8
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,360
Does the wolf know you?

9
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,900
We need all the help we can get.

10
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:18,510
Ser Davos.

11
00:06:00,990 --> 00:06:02,650
I saw him in the flames

12
00:06:04,270 --> 00:06:05,920
fighting at Winterfell.

13
00:06:10,650 --> 00:06:12,450
I can't speak for the flames...

14
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,410
but he's gone.

15
00:06:36,490 --> 00:06:38,530
He was our Lord Commander.

16
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:40,260
He never should have been!

17
00:06:43,830 --> 00:06:45,790
You all know why you're here.

18
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:51,670
Jon Snow is dead.

19
00:06:51,670 --> 00:06:52,740
Who killed him?

20
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:55,020
I did.

21
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:58,770
And Bowen Marsh and Othell Yarwyck

22
00:06:58,770 --> 00:07:00,710
and the other officers in this castle.

23
00:07:00,710 --> 00:07:02,730
- Murderers! - Traitors!

24
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:07,720
You're right!

25
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:10,690
We've committed treason, all of us.

26
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:13,650
Jon Snow was my Lord Commander.

27
00:07:14,930 --> 00:07:16,620
I had no love for him.

28
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:18,440
That was no secret.

29
00:07:19,330 --> 00:07:23,020
But I never once disobeyed an order.

30
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:28,210
Loyalty is the foundation on which the Night's Watch is built.

31
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,660
And the Watch means everything to me.

32
00:07:31,010 --> 00:07:32,770
I have given my life,

33
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:36,820
we have all given our lives to the Night's Watch.

34
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:44,020
Jon Snow was going to destroy the Night's Watch.

35
00:07:44,230 --> 00:07:46,820
He let the wildlings through our gates

36
00:07:46,820 --> 00:07:49,830
as no Lord Commander has ever done before.

37
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:54,870
He gave them the very land on which they reaved

38
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:57,660
and raped and murdered.

39
00:07:59,150 --> 00:08:03,030
Lord Commander Snow did what he thought was right,

40
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,660
I've no doubt about that.

41
00:08:06,330 --> 00:08:10,320
And what he thought was right would have been the end of us.

42
00:08:10,730 --> 00:08:13,230
He thrust a terrible choice upon us.

43
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:15,970
And we made it.

44
00:08:28,810 --> 00:08:30,600
He'll have seen we didn't come.

45
00:08:31,110 --> 00:08:33,180
Thorne will have made it official by now.

46
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:34,470
Castle Black is his.

47
00:08:34,470 --> 00:08:37,220
I don't care who's sitting at the high table.

48
00:08:38,130 --> 00:08:39,450
Jon was my friend.

49
00:08:41,030 --> 00:08:42,920
And those fuckers butchered him.

50
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:45,270
Now we return the favor.

51
00:08:45,270 --> 00:08:46,890
We don't have the numbers.

52
00:08:46,950 --> 00:08:49,120
- We have a direwolf. - It's not enough.

53
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:51,420
I didn't know Lord Commander Snow for long,

54
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:52,150
but I have to believe

55
00:08:52,150 --> 00:08:54,480
he wouldn't have wanted his friends to die for nothing.

56
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:57,880
If you were planning to see tomorrow, you picked the wrong room.

57
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:00,710
We all die today.

58
00:09:01,570 --> 00:09:04,610
I say we do our best to take Thorne with us when we go.

59
00:09:04,610 --> 00:09:07,610
We need to fight, but we don't need to die.

60
00:09:07,610 --> 00:09:10,160
- Not if we have help. - Who is gonna help us?

61
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:13,380
You're not the only ones who owe your lives to Jon Snow.

62
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:23,170
Bolt the door.

63
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:25,010
Don't let anyone in.

64
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:27,190
I'll be back as soon as I can.

65
00:09:38,070 --> 00:09:40,350
She was 11 the first time I saw her.

66
00:09:43,170 --> 00:09:45,170
The kennelmaster's daughter.

67
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:49,640
She smelled of dog.

68
00:09:53,740 --> 00:09:56,860
I wasn't much older, but everybody was already afraid of me.

69
00:09:58,830 --> 00:10:00,240
You certainly were.

70
00:10:06,330 --> 00:10:07,830
Myranda wasn't, though.

71
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:11,130
What could I do to her that those hounds couldn't?

72
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,350
She was fearless.

73
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:15,950
There was nothing she wouldn't do.

74
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:25,750
Your pain will be paid for a thousand times over.

75
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:31,260
I wish you could be here to watch.

76
00:10:36,230 --> 00:10:39,370
Shall I have a grave dug for her, my lord?

77
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,640
Or would you rather the men build a pyre?

78
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:50,410
Buried, burned?

79
00:10:51,850 --> 00:10:52,910
This is good meat.

80
00:10:52,910 --> 00:10:54,250
Feed it to the hounds.

81
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:59,150
Your command of the cavalry was impressive.

82
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:02,530
Thanks to you, the false king Stannis Baratheon is dead.

83
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:04,550
Do you know who struck the killing blow?

84
00:11:05,050 --> 00:11:06,810
- No. - A shame.

85
00:11:07,030 --> 00:11:08,410
I'd reward the man.

86
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:11,750
Still, a great victory.

87
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:14,370
Do you feel like a victor?

88
00:11:20,030 --> 00:11:21,390
I rebelled against the crown

89
00:11:21,390 --> 00:11:23,910
to arrange your marriage to Sansa Stark.

90
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,290
Do you think that burning wagons in the night

91
00:11:26,290 --> 00:11:28,690
and mowing down tired, outnumbered Baratheons

92
00:11:28,690 --> 00:11:30,330
is the same as facing a prepared

93
00:11:30,330 --> 00:11:32,370
and provisioned Lannister army?

94
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,000
No.

95
00:11:38,590 --> 00:11:39,980
A reckoning will come.

96
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:41,960
We need the North to face it.

97
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:43,620
The entire North.

98
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:47,110
They won't back us without Sansa Stark.

99
00:11:48,590 --> 00:11:50,630
We no longer have Sansa Stark.

100
00:11:51,350 --> 00:11:52,970
You played your games with her.

101
00:11:53,450 --> 00:11:55,670
You played your games with the heir to the Iron Islands

102
00:11:55,670 --> 00:11:56,920
and now they're both gone.

103
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,940
I have a team of men after them with some of my best hounds.

104
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,410
They won't get far.

105
00:12:01,410 --> 00:12:02,660
I'm glad to hear it.

106
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:06,370
Without Sansa, you won't be able to produce an heir.

107
00:12:07,010 --> 00:12:09,990
And without an heir, well...

108
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,920
let's hope the maesters are right

109
00:12:15,010 --> 00:12:16,960
and Lady Walda's carrying a boy.

110
00:12:37,990 --> 00:12:39,120
We can't stop.

111
00:12:58,550 --> 00:12:59,820
We have to cross here.

112
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:05,590
- I can't. - It's the only way to throw off the hounds.

113
00:13:05,590 --> 00:13:08,490
But it's too cold. I can't. I won't make it. I'll die.

114
00:13:08,490 --> 00:13:10,790
I've seen what his hounds do to a person.

115
00:13:10,850 --> 00:13:12,390
This way is better.

116
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:47,220
Over here. Come on.

117
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:04,030
Sansa.

118
00:14:05,510 --> 00:14:06,540
Sansa.

119
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:28,940
Tell them to settle down!

120
00:14:30,450 --> 00:14:31,940
Stay here. I'll lure them away.

121
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,940
No, I won't make it without you.

122
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:35,050
You will.

123
00:14:35,830 --> 00:14:38,050
Go north, only north.

124
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:40,420
Jon is Lord Commander at Castle Black.

125
00:14:41,050 --> 00:14:42,170
He'll help you.

126
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:52,580
See somebody, eh?

127
00:14:53,630 --> 00:14:55,490
- There they are! - Get them!

128
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:02,290
Where is Lady Bolton?

129
00:15:03,570 --> 00:15:05,370
- Dead. - Liar.

130
00:15:06,330 --> 00:15:08,540
She broke her leg jumping from the ramparts.

131
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,670
I left her to die in the snow.

132
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:17,590
Got something! Run!

133
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:32,160
Resist. Stay.

134
00:15:35,510 --> 00:15:36,610
Stay.

135
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:39,800
I can't wait to see what parts Ramsay cuts off you this time.

136
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,340
Rider!

137
00:15:50,970 --> 00:15:52,390
- Who is it? - It's a bloody woman.

138
00:17:00,970 --> 00:17:03,170
No! Please! No!

139
00:17:56,350 --> 00:17:59,490
Lady Sansa, I offer my services once again.

140
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:03,310
I will shield your back and keep your counsel

141
00:18:03,310 --> 00:18:05,600
and give my life for yours if need be.

142
00:18:07,050 --> 00:18:09,380
I swear it by the old gods and the new.

143
00:18:19,570 --> 00:18:20,790
And I vow...

144
00:18:23,390 --> 00:18:26,410
that you shall always have a place by my hearth

145
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:28,330
and...

146
00:18:30,850 --> 00:18:32,270
Meat and mead at my table.

147
00:18:32,270 --> 00:18:34,580
meat and mead at my table.

148
00:18:37,570 --> 00:18:41,780
And I pledge to ask no service of you

149
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:43,870
that might bring you dishonor.

150
00:18:45,010 --> 00:18:47,510
I swear it by the old gods and the new.

151
00:18:49,490 --> 00:18:50,600
Arise.

152
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:39,300
Your Grace, I'm sorry to disturb you.

153
00:19:39,570 --> 00:19:41,680
A ship from Dorne has sailed into the harbor.

154
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:44,730
Myrcella.

155
00:20:58,290 --> 00:21:00,660
Do you remember the first time you saw a dead body?

156
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:03,490
Mother.

157
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:08,110
All I could think about when she died

158
00:21:08,110 --> 00:21:10,090
was what would happen to her now.

159
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:15,840
Every day, every night,

160
00:21:17,270 --> 00:21:19,160
what does Mama look like now?

161
00:21:21,980 --> 00:21:23,800
Has she started to bloat?

162
00:21:25,860 --> 00:21:27,830
Has her skin turned black?

163
00:21:29,910 --> 00:21:32,010
Have her lips peeled back from her teeth?

164
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:40,240
I think about locking Myrcella in a crypt.

165
00:21:41,990 --> 00:21:44,550
I think about her beautiful little face starting to collapse.

166
00:21:44,550 --> 00:21:47,100
Don't think about it.

167
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:49,430
I have to.

168
00:21:51,710 --> 00:21:53,830
I have to. It's not right she has to suffer alone.

169
00:21:53,830 --> 00:21:56,090
She's not suffering. She's gone.

170
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:59,330
No one can hurt her anymore.

171
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:03,130
She was good.

172
00:22:04,930 --> 00:22:07,520
From her first breath, she was so sweet.

173
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:11,260
I don't know where she came from.

174
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:15,130
She was nothing like me.

175
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:19,160
No meanness, no jealousy, just good.

176
00:22:19,170 --> 00:22:20,200
I know.

177
00:22:21,180 --> 00:22:24,060
I thought if I could make something so good,

178
00:22:26,090 --> 00:22:27,420
so pure...

179
00:22:30,420 --> 00:22:33,090
- Maybe I'm not a monster. - Listen-- listen to me.

180
00:22:33,090 --> 00:22:35,880
She was my daughter and I failed her.

181
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:37,570
No, I knew this would happen.

182
00:22:38,530 --> 00:22:40,340
The witch told me years ago.

183
00:22:42,380 --> 00:22:45,280
She promised me three children and she promised me they'd die.

184
00:22:45,850 --> 00:22:47,550
"And gold their shrouds."

185
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:49,940
Everything she said came true.

186
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:51,640
You couldn't have stopped it.

187
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,500
It's prophecy. It's fate.

188
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:55,790
- You don't believe that. - Of course I do.

189
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:59,340
You told me yourself when Father died.

190
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:02,130
You said we had to stay together.

191
00:23:02,260 --> 00:23:05,250
You said people would try to tear us apart, take what's ours.

192
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,470
That was a prophecy, too.

193
00:23:06,470 --> 00:23:09,230
I didn't listen to you and everything you said came true.

194
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:11,770
Fuck prophecy. Fuck fate.

195
00:23:11,770 --> 00:23:13,620
Fuck everyone who isn't us.

196
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:15,810
We're the only ones who matter,

197
00:23:15,810 --> 00:23:17,530
the only ones in this world.

198
00:23:18,130 --> 00:23:19,480
And everything they've taken from us,

199
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:21,600
we're going to take back and more.

200
00:23:24,540 --> 00:23:26,700
We're going to take everything there is.

201
00:23:34,270 --> 00:23:37,490
"The Seven Hells brim with the souls of saintly men.

202
00:23:38,050 --> 00:23:40,950
They scream in agony and their shame is so great,

203
00:23:40,950 --> 00:23:42,840
they do not feel the flames,

204
00:23:43,090 --> 00:23:47,350
for now they see if not for a single sin they concealed,

205
00:23:47,410 --> 00:23:48,690
they were saved."

206
00:23:49,020 --> 00:23:50,410
I'd like to see my brother.

207
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:52,800
- Confess. - Please.

208
00:23:53,610 --> 00:23:55,410
How is he? At least tell me that.

209
00:23:55,410 --> 00:23:56,590
Confess.

210
00:24:00,620 --> 00:24:02,830
I am the queen and I demand to see my brother.

211
00:24:02,830 --> 00:24:04,700
Sinners don't make demands.

212
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:07,340
They make confessions.

213
00:24:11,080 --> 00:24:12,960
Septa Unella.

214
00:24:14,930 --> 00:24:16,960
Our other guests need you.

215
00:24:28,150 --> 00:24:29,350
There.

216
00:24:31,500 --> 00:24:34,660
Septa Unella can be overzealous at times.

217
00:24:34,900 --> 00:24:36,370
I'll speak with her.

218
00:24:38,030 --> 00:24:41,130
My brother, can you tell me how he is?

219
00:24:42,850 --> 00:24:46,620
It isn't Ser Loras that brings me here.

220
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:50,170
Your husband misses you dearly.

221
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:53,690
The love between a man and wife is sacred.

222
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:57,450
It reflects the love the gods have for all of us.

223
00:24:57,540 --> 00:25:01,410
But sin leads us away from the sacred.

224
00:25:02,230 --> 00:25:04,970
And only confession can purge sin.

225
00:25:05,470 --> 00:25:07,930
I have nothing to confess.

226
00:25:08,530 --> 00:25:11,690
So you believe you are pure?

227
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:13,730
Perfect?

228
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:16,060
Wholly without sin?

229
00:25:17,940 --> 00:25:19,320
None of us are.

230
00:25:21,470 --> 00:25:23,610
You have started down the path.

231
00:25:25,470 --> 00:25:27,660
But you have many miles to go.

232
00:25:41,710 --> 00:25:43,830
I always envied Oberyn.

233
00:25:44,590 --> 00:25:46,070
He lived.

234
00:25:46,520 --> 00:25:47,750
He truly lived.

235
00:25:47,760 --> 00:25:49,510
Sailed around the world.

236
00:25:49,620 --> 00:25:51,680
Fought men from every country.

237
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:54,300
Lay with the most beautiful women alive.

238
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:56,240
- And men. - And men.

239
00:25:56,350 --> 00:25:58,440
He experienced everything

240
00:25:59,090 --> 00:26:02,160
while I sat here in Dorne

241
00:26:02,180 --> 00:26:06,140
trying my best to keep my people alive and well fed.

242
00:26:07,080 --> 00:26:08,680
But that is life.

243
00:26:10,380 --> 00:26:12,380
We each have our roles.

244
00:26:12,770 --> 00:26:16,870
Oberyn was born to be an adventurer.

245
00:26:17,550 --> 00:26:19,640
And I was born to rule.

246
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:21,620
The gods are not fools.

247
00:26:21,790 --> 00:26:24,080
You would have been a lousy adventurer.

248
00:26:24,390 --> 00:26:26,210
And Oberyn, pfft,

249
00:26:27,090 --> 00:26:29,110
he would have been a terrible ruler.

250
00:26:29,910 --> 00:26:32,710
Your mother is a brilliant woman, you know that?

251
00:26:32,900 --> 00:26:34,350
Prince Doran.

252
00:26:46,510 --> 00:26:48,280
The Princess Myrcella.

253
00:27:07,380 --> 00:27:09,890
When was the last time you left this palace?

254
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:12,360
You don't know your own people.

255
00:27:12,790 --> 00:27:14,730
Their disgust for you.

256
00:27:15,390 --> 00:27:19,050
Elia Martell raped and murdered, and you did nothing.

257
00:27:19,840 --> 00:27:24,090
Oberyn Martell butchered, and you did nothing.

258
00:27:25,650 --> 00:27:27,540
You're not a Dornishman.

259
00:27:29,320 --> 00:27:31,250
You're not our prince.

260
00:27:31,990 --> 00:27:35,860
My son Trystane...

261
00:27:37,310 --> 00:27:40,950
Your son is weak just like you.

262
00:27:41,340 --> 00:27:44,640
And weak men will never rule Dorne again.

263
00:28:07,490 --> 00:28:09,670
I told you I'm not hungry.

264
00:28:09,930 --> 00:28:12,020
We're not here to feed you.

265
00:28:14,540 --> 00:28:16,210
We're here to kill you.

266
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:19,360
You want her to do it or me?

267
00:28:19,480 --> 00:28:22,270
We are family. I don't want to hurt you.

268
00:28:22,840 --> 00:28:25,760
Her or me?

269
00:28:30,520 --> 00:28:31,780
You.

270
00:28:32,080 --> 00:28:33,160
Good.

271
00:28:33,650 --> 00:28:35,080
Smart boy.

272
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:54,690
You're a greedy bitch, you know that?

273
00:29:03,550 --> 00:29:05,490
We're never going to fix what's wrong with this city

274
00:29:05,490 --> 00:29:07,560
from the top of an 800-foot pyramid.

275
00:29:09,020 --> 00:29:10,540
We'll be fine.

276
00:29:10,930 --> 00:29:13,000
We're dressed like common merchants.

277
00:29:14,770 --> 00:29:16,670
You walk like a rich person.

278
00:29:17,300 --> 00:29:20,510
You've spent a lot of time studying the way rich people walk?

279
00:29:20,510 --> 00:29:24,330
You walk as though the paving stones were your personal property.

280
00:29:24,750 --> 00:29:27,580
I used to steal from people like you when I was a boy.

281
00:29:27,580 --> 00:29:29,620
It's a good thing you're not a boy anymore.

282
00:29:31,350 --> 00:29:33,160
Because you have no cock.

283
00:29:51,860 --> 00:29:54,110
She thinks you want to eat her baby.

284
00:30:17,010 --> 00:30:20,650
- Mhysa means mother in Valyrian. - I know what mhysa means.

285
00:30:20,650 --> 00:30:23,030
- Who wrote it? - Hard to know.

286
00:30:23,030 --> 00:30:26,410
Our queen is not as popular in Meereen as she used to be.

287
00:30:26,410 --> 00:30:28,060
The Sons of the Harpy?

288
00:30:28,070 --> 00:30:29,660
Very possibly.

289
00:30:31,470 --> 00:30:34,430
Daenerys Targaryen took away their most valuable property,

290
00:30:34,670 --> 00:30:37,770
told them human beings weren't even property to begin with.

291
00:30:38,830 --> 00:30:40,890
You can see why they're unhappy.

292
00:30:41,980 --> 00:30:43,390
Of course,

293
00:30:44,020 --> 00:30:45,960
it could also be the freed men.

294
00:30:57,990 --> 00:31:00,840
Many of the former slaves feel that Daenerys has abandoned them.

295
00:31:01,130 --> 00:31:04,430
She did fly away on a dragon and not come back.

296
00:31:22,550 --> 00:31:24,060
It's a problem.

297
00:31:25,980 --> 00:31:28,650
Fear has brought Meereen to a standstill.

298
00:31:30,510 --> 00:31:32,900
Whoever you are, wherever you go,

299
00:31:33,150 --> 00:31:35,740
someone in this city wants to murder you.

300
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:38,760
We can't fight an enemy we don't know.

301
00:31:39,820 --> 00:31:42,470
The Sons of the Harpy planned their attack

302
00:31:42,470 --> 00:31:44,560
in the fighting pits very carefully,

303
00:31:44,560 --> 00:31:47,170
which means they take orders from someone.

304
00:31:47,320 --> 00:31:49,700
And have you started looking for that someone?

305
00:31:49,700 --> 00:31:52,270
My little birds have already taken wing.

306
00:31:52,280 --> 00:31:53,730
Soon they'll return,

307
00:31:53,730 --> 00:31:57,010
singing songs of men in gold masks.

308
00:32:30,850 --> 00:32:35,280
Well, we won't be sailing to Westeros anytime soon.

309
00:32:57,860 --> 00:32:59,010
Goat?

310
00:32:59,440 --> 00:33:00,640
Ram.

311
00:33:01,110 --> 00:33:02,780
You think our friend got him?

312
00:33:04,480 --> 00:33:07,330
Don't know anything else that can melt a ram's horn.

313
00:33:09,470 --> 00:33:11,240
We're on the right path, then.

314
00:33:12,420 --> 00:33:14,840
Perhaps she's tired of being queen.

315
00:33:14,930 --> 00:33:16,920
I don't think she likes it very much.

316
00:33:17,150 --> 00:33:18,960
She's too smart to like it.

317
00:33:19,420 --> 00:33:21,170
Maybe she's flown somewhere else,

318
00:33:21,170 --> 00:33:23,530
somewhere far away from men like us.

319
00:33:24,210 --> 00:33:26,170
I've been all over the world.

320
00:33:26,300 --> 00:33:28,430
There's no escaping men like us.

321
00:33:28,430 --> 00:33:30,590
There's no escaping her, eh?

322
00:33:31,270 --> 00:33:33,550
You keep coming back. Why?

323
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:35,770
You know why.

324
00:33:37,810 --> 00:33:39,440
Isn't it frustrating

325
00:33:39,990 --> 00:33:42,190
wanting someone who doesn't want you back?

326
00:33:43,650 --> 00:33:45,130
Of course it is.

327
00:33:45,150 --> 00:33:47,830
You're a romantic. I admire that.

328
00:33:48,040 --> 00:33:49,760
Sometimes I look at you and I think,

329
00:33:49,760 --> 00:33:52,040
"So that's what I'll be like when I grow old."

330
00:33:52,390 --> 00:33:53,940
If you grow old.

331
00:33:53,940 --> 00:33:55,520
If I grow old.

332
00:33:56,150 --> 00:33:57,610
I hope I do.

333
00:33:57,930 --> 00:33:59,440
I want to see what the world looks like

334
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:01,050
when she's done conquering it.

335
00:34:01,450 --> 00:34:02,840
So do I.

336
00:34:23,710 --> 00:34:25,350
Huh, an army?

337
00:34:25,670 --> 00:34:27,110
Not an army.

338
00:34:27,340 --> 00:34:28,710
A horde.

339
00:34:54,850 --> 00:34:56,170
Dothraki?

340
00:35:19,490 --> 00:35:20,850
They have her.

341
00:37:27,040 --> 00:37:27,840
No.

342
00:41:52,650 --> 00:41:54,980
But there has to be a price to pay for everything.

343
00:41:55,060 --> 00:41:58,640
I know, but have you tried telling him that?

344
00:42:06,040 --> 00:42:06,980
Thank you.

345
00:42:09,930 --> 00:42:11,580
Who'd go there after what happened to that Kingsguard?

346
00:42:11,580 --> 00:42:13,450
- Probably had it coming. - Maybe so,

347
00:42:13,450 --> 00:42:14,640
but I'm not risking it.

348
00:42:14,640 --> 00:42:16,370
- Just can't do it. - All right.

349
00:42:16,370 --> 00:42:18,620
Honesty as well. He gets it.

350
00:42:23,590 --> 00:42:25,220
Are you listening, blind girl?

351
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:28,680
Do you hear them talking?

352
00:42:29,950 --> 00:42:31,540
Do any of them talk to you?

353
00:42:32,940 --> 00:42:33,760
No.

354
00:42:35,500 --> 00:42:36,710
So sad.

355
00:42:44,730 --> 00:42:46,450
Stand and fight, blind girl.

356
00:42:48,230 --> 00:42:49,190
I can't see.

357
00:42:49,190 --> 00:42:51,300
That's your problem, not mine.

358
00:43:19,870 --> 00:43:21,050
See you tomorrow.

359
00:44:13,430 --> 00:44:16,730
Ser Davos, we have no cause to fight.

360
00:44:17,670 --> 00:44:19,800
We are both anointed knights.

361
00:44:19,890 --> 00:44:23,100
Hear that, lads? Nothing to fear.

362
00:44:23,100 --> 00:44:25,490
I will grant amnesty to all brothers

363
00:44:25,490 --> 00:44:28,010
who throw down their arms before nightfall.

364
00:44:28,020 --> 00:44:31,790
And you, Ser Davos, I will allow you to travel south

365
00:44:31,950 --> 00:44:34,450
a free man with a fresh horse.

366
00:44:36,240 --> 00:44:37,500
And some mutton.

367
00:44:38,550 --> 00:44:39,830
I'd like some mutton.

368
00:44:40,130 --> 00:44:42,730
- What? - I'm not much of a hunter.

369
00:44:44,060 --> 00:44:47,690
I'll need some food if I'm gonna make it south without starving.

370
00:44:51,400 --> 00:44:52,770
We'll give you food.

371
00:44:53,720 --> 00:44:56,350
You can bring the Red Woman with you if you like.

372
00:44:57,380 --> 00:45:00,570
Or you can leave her here with us, whichever you choose.

373
00:45:00,910 --> 00:45:05,460
But surrender by nightfall or this ends with blood.

374
00:45:06,920 --> 00:45:08,410
Thank you, Ser Alliser.

375
00:45:09,150 --> 00:45:10,760
We'll discuss amongst ourselves

376
00:45:10,760 --> 00:45:12,470
and come back to you with an answer.

377
00:45:28,110 --> 00:45:31,480
Boys, I've been running from men like that all my life.

378
00:45:32,400 --> 00:45:35,750
In my learned opinion, we open that door--

379
00:45:35,750 --> 00:45:37,170
And they'll slaughter us all.

380
00:45:37,170 --> 00:45:39,600
- They want to come in. - They're gonna come in.

381
00:45:39,600 --> 00:45:41,820
Aye, but we don't need to make it easy for them.

382
00:45:41,820 --> 00:45:43,280
Edd is our only chance.

383
00:45:43,280 --> 00:45:46,740
It's a sad fucking statement if Dolorous Edd is our only chance.

384
00:45:48,820 --> 00:45:50,080
There's always the Red Woman.

385
00:45:50,090 --> 00:45:53,240
What's one redhead gonna do against 40 armed men?

386
00:45:54,480 --> 00:45:56,580
You haven't seen her do what I've seen her do.

